---
title: Custom Payment Gateway
description: Accept manual payments such as bank transfers, checks, cash, or other offline workflows.
---

The Custom gateway shows clients how to pay by bank transfer, check, or another manual method. For automated payment integrations, see [Creating a Payment Gateway](/extensions-and-development/guides/creating-a-payment-gateway/).

## Configure the Gateway

In the admin panel, go to **System → Payment Gateways** and open **Custom**. To install the bundled adapter, select **New Payment Gateway** and find **Custom** under **Available Adapters**.

Editing payment instructions requires the **Manage payment gateways** permission.

Enable the gateway and select the payment types and currencies you accept. Leave **Accepted Currencies** empty to allow all currencies. Enter instructions in **Single Payment Information** for one-time payments or **Subscription Information** for recurring payments.

## Example: Bank Transfer Instructions

Use the `invoice` variable to show the amount, currency, or invoice number. Replace the sample bank details with your own.

```twig {% process=false %}
<p>Transfer {{ invoice.total }} {{ invoice.currency }} to Example Bank (IBAN GB00 XXXX 0000 0000 0000 00).</p>
<p>Use {{ invoice.serie_nr }} as the payment reference.</p>
```

FOSSBilling renders the instructions in a Twig sandbox and sanitizes the resulting HTML. The sandbox supports basic expressions, conditions, and loops. It rejects template imports, includes, API calls, and debugging helpers such as `dump()`.

## Mark an Invoice as Paid

After verifying the payment, open the unpaid invoice from **Invoices → Overview**.

{% steps %}
1. In **Manage → Billing Settings**, set **Payment Method** to your Custom gateway and select **Update Invoice**.
2. On the **Details** tab, select **Mark as Paid**. Enter the payment reference in **Transaction ID** and select **Submit**.
{% /steps %}

FOSSBilling requires the transaction ID for Custom payments. It records the transaction, marks the invoice as paid, and runs the related invoice tasks.
